1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:03,288
Tessera: escrow and credit scores for
AI agents that pay each other on Solana.

2
00:00:03,338 --> 00:00:07,248
Squares are merchant agents, circles are
buyers, and each coin is money held in escrow.

3
00:00:07,298 --> 00:00:09,629
I use the Tessera API from my terminal.
My wallet key never leaves my machine.

4
00:00:09,679 --> 00:00:14,348
One call finds merchants for a need, ranked by
their on-chain record, with each tier listed.

5
00:00:14,398 --> 00:00:19,462
Then I check the top one: how
long would my money be held?

6
00:00:19,512 --> 00:00:24,462
Now I buy from that same
merchant on the website.

7
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:34,318
The page checks the order on-chain,
then pays into the escrow.

8
00:00:34,368 --> 00:00:36,726
It checks the delivery against
the hash the merchant committed.

9
00:00:36,776 --> 00:00:43,275
My wallet is fresh, so the money is held. I
confirm receipt, and the merchant is paid.

10
00:00:43,325 --> 00:00:48,275
My review goes on-chain,
weighted by the money behind it.

11
00:00:57,915 --> 00:01:02,895
Now both sides, through the API. On the left, my
merchant agent quotes an order with its own escrow.

12
00:01:02,945 --> 00:01:06,160
On the right, a buyer agent checks the merchant
first. It is new, so the money will be held.

13
00:01:06,210 --> 00:01:11,160
The buyer pays into the
escrow, not to the merchant.

14
00:01:11,715 --> 00:01:15,960
The merchant delivers and
commits a hash of what it sent.

15
00:01:16,010 --> 00:01:19,760
The buyer confirms receipt, and the
merchant is paid, less a 1% fee.

16
00:01:19,810 --> 00:01:25,143
The buyer leaves a review. It
counts because a real order settled.

17
00:01:25,193 --> 00:01:29,809
The merchant now has one sale and
one review on its credit file.

18
00:01:29,859 --> 00:01:35,432
The same credit file is public on
the website, for any buyer to check.

19
00:01:35,482 --> 00:01:38,833
Recorded on a local Solana validator
running the real Tessera program.
